# Trivy ignore policy for GitPreserver
#
# List CVE/vulnerability IDs here to suppress accepted findings from the
# image vulnerability scan (see .github/workflows/lint.yml -> trivy job).
#
# Rules:
#   - One vulnerability ID per line (e.g. CVE-2024-12345).
#   - Every suppression MUST have an explanatory comment above it stating
#     WHY it is accepted and WHO/WHEN reviewed it. Undocumented suppressions
#     are not allowed and should be removed during review.
#   - Prefer fixing or upgrading over ignoring. Ignore only when the finding
#     is a false positive, not reachable in this image, or has no available
#     fix and the risk is formally accepted.
#   - Optionally add an expiry note so stale suppressions get re-reviewed.
#
# Example:
#   # CVE-2025-0001: false positive, the vulnerable codepath in libfoo is not
#   # invoked by GitPreserver. Accepted by @dougeubanks on 2026-06-11.
#   # CVE-2025-0001
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go stdlib CVEs in upstream-prebuilt binaries (ghorg, supercronic)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are reported against the Go standard library compiled INTO the third-
# party release binaries we bundle (usr/local/bin/ghorg, usr/local/bin/
# supercronic), not against any code or package we control. We already pin the
# latest upstream releases (ghorg 1.11.11, supercronic 0.2.46); the only real
# fix is for those projects to recompile with a patched Go toolchain and cut a
# new release. gh and rclone report zero — they ship with a current Go.
#
# Risk is low for a backup tool: ghorg/supercronic process our own config and
# git URLs, not untrusted network input. Re-review and prune this list whenever
# ghorg or supercronic is bumped (Dependabot/manual). Accepted by @dougeubanks
# on 2026-06-12.
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-27137
CVE-2026-27142
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33810
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39823
CVE-2026-39825
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
CVE-2026-42504
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additional Go module CVEs in upstream-prebuilt binaries (gh, ghorg, supercronic)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# New findings from the 2026-07-01 scan against the same pinned binaries.
# All are in golang.org/x/crypto, golang.org/x/net, Go stdlib, or
# github.com/sigstore/rekor compiled into the prebuilt gh/ghorg/supercronic
# releases we bundle. None of these libraries are called by GitPreserver code
# directly. Re-review whenever gh, ghorg, or supercronic is bumped.
# Accepted by @dougeubanks on 2026-07-01.
#
# golang.org/x/crypto (ghorg): SSH client DoS conditions — ghorg uses SSH for
# git operations against our own repos, not as a server.
CVE-2026-39827
CVE-2026-39828
CVE-2026-39829
CVE-2026-39830
CVE-2026-39832
CVE-2026-39835
CVE-2026-42508
CVE-2026-46595
CVE-2026-46597
# golang.org/x/net (ghorg): HTML parser and IDNA issues — not reachable in
# a git-cloning workflow.
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-42502
# Go stdlib crypto/x509 (ghorg, supercronic): DoS in certificate parsing —
# neither binary is serving TLS connections from untrusted clients.
CVE-2026-27145
# github.com/sigstore/rekor (gh): OOM via unbounded gzip decompression in the
# Sigstore transparency-log client bundled inside the gh CLI binary. GitPreserver
# does not use gh for signature verification; the rekor client is never invoked.
CVE-2026-48702
